# Citations

Use **Vancouver / NLM numeric** (citation-sequence). In-text numbers, numbered list at the end. That is the biomedical default and matches existing notes such as the clocks article.

Do not use APA/Harvard author-date in running text. Do not use MLA.

## How

Each article that cites sources:

- `bibliography: references.bib` in the article YAML (file lives next to `index.qmd`)
- Site CSL is already set in `articles/_metadata.yml` (`csl/vancouver.csl`)
- Cite with Pandoc keys: `[@ley2011course]` or `[@kipf2017gcn; @velickovic2018gat]`. In-text form is square brackets (`[1]`), matching older hand-numbered notes.
- End the article with:

```markdown
## References

::: {#refs}
:::
```

Cite load-bearing claims (epidemiology, trials, methods papers, databases). Skip citations on the project's own CV numbers.

Older articles that already use a hand-numbered `[1]` list may keep that list until they are edited; new work uses BibTeX plus this CSL.
